  <div class="detail">A {corr_val} correlation between rating gap and higher-rated player winning. A 200-point gap yields ~70% win probability for the stronger player; 400+ points pushes it above 80%. This relationship is near-monotonic across all bin sizes, confirming Elo's predictive validity on Lichess.</div>
</div>

<div class="finding-box">
  <strong>Resignation dominates game endings; checkmate is relatively rare.</strong>
  <div class="detail">{pct(victory_data.get('resign',0), total_games)}% of games end by resignation vs. only {checkmate_rate}% by checkmate. This reflects modern chess culture: players resign lost positions rather than playing to mate. However, in bullet, timeouts ({pct(victory_data.get('outoftime',0), total_games)}% overall) rise significantly as clock management becomes critical.</div>
</div>

<div class="finding-box">
